{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792253660,"nonce":"ZzzstGk7cp3kZwYjLP4fHNTK6Fo=","title":"Python: comparing an instance with a value of another kind overflows the stack","message":"`zb_any_eq` on an instance and a non-instance (`Money(4) == 3`, a value of `[Plain(), 3][i]` compared with `\"s\"`) calls the instance eq hook, whose identity fallback calls `zb_any_same`, then `zb_any_is`, which falls through to the value comparison and calls `zb_any_eq` again. The process aborts with \"thread has overflowed its stack\".\n\n`zb_any_is` must answer false when exactly one side is a heap object: such a value is never identical to a value of another category.\n\nReproducer: `crates/zyntax_python/conformance/class/instance_truth_and_equality.py`.","files":null}]}